<title>UK: HSBC shares fall after results.</title>
<headline>HSBC shares fall after results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in banking group HSBC Holdings Plc were indicated lower on Monday after a group profit rise of 23 percent to 4.52 billion stg fell within expectations.</p>
<p>The shares were off 38-1/2p at 15.43-1/2 stg by 0818 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;The figures looked quite respectable,&quot; said one trader. &quot;But they closed easier in Hong Kong on a bit of nervousness ahead of results.&quot;  </p>
<p>Annual pretax profits of 4.5 billion stg met with analysts consensus forecasts. A total dividend of 41p/shr was higher than most analysts expected.</p>
<p>In Hong Kong on Monday the shares slipped on profit-taking ahead of the earnings.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
</text>
